Logs.Reasoning:
All length‑3 negatives are exactly the triples where the third symbol is not allowed after the preceding two symbols. The allowed continuations are:
- after “ab”, only “a”;
- after “ac”, only “a”;
- after “ba”, only “a”;
- after “ca”, only “a”;
- after “cb”, only “a” or “b”;
- after “bc”, only “b” or “c”;
- after “aa”, only “a”;
- after “bb” or “cc”, any symbol.  
Thus the language consists of strings whose every length‑3 factor obeys these rules.
